WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.679
Content often starts in a spreadsheet.

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:08.428
This video shows how bulk import and export move many content items into

00:00:08.428 --> 00:00:11.898
your site, and out of it, with a CSV or Excel file:

00:00:11.898 --> 00:00:16.099
why they exist, how to prepare a file, how to follow an import,

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.560
and how to export.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.753
Content often starts in a spreadsheet:

00:00:24.753 --> 00:00:29.056
a purchased list of leads, records from an older system, or a price

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:31.590
list that a colleague keeps in Excel.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.141
Typing hundreds of rows into forms, one at a time, is slow, and

00:00:37.141 --> 00:00:40.550
every row is a chance for a typing mistake.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.368
Bulk import creates or updates many content items from one file, and checks

00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:50.560
every row the same way as when someone saves an item by hand.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.464
Bulk export does the reverse.

00:00:53.464 --> 00:00:57.403
It downloads content items to a file that you can fix in a

00:00:57.403 --> 00:01:01.650
spreadsheet, hand to someone outside the site, or import again.

00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:08.592
Both tools are under the Content menu.

00:01:08.592 --> 00:01:13.811
Import opens the Bulk Import page, which lists every import made on the site.

00:01:13.811 --> 00:01:15.445
It is empty for now.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:21.537
Export opens the Bulk Export page, which lists every export in the same way.

00:01:21.537 --> 00:01:24.561
Its Export button starts a new export.

00:01:28.774 --> 00:01:32.950
Every content type is offered on these pages by default.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:39.954
To change that, open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit a type, such as Customer.

00:01:40.408 --> 00:01:45.346
Allow bulk import and Allow bulk export decide whether the type appears on

00:01:45.346 --> 00:01:48.555
the Bulk Import page and the Bulk Export page.

00:01:48.555 --> 00:01:51.518
Untick one to keep the type off that page.

00:01:55.738 --> 00:02:00.371
On the Bulk Import page, click Import to see every content type that

00:02:00.371 --> 00:02:02.938
can be imported, and pick Customer.

00:02:03.388 --> 00:02:07.888
The File Requirements card says what the file must look like.

00:02:07.888 --> 00:02:12.454
It uses one of the enabled formats, here CSV or Excel, and its

00:02:12.454 --> 00:02:15.408
very first row holds the column names.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.710
The order of the columns does not matter, and a column the type

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.440
does not know is ignored.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.680
To start with the right columns, download a template in either format.

00:02:26.161 --> 00:02:32.271
The Columns Requirements table lists every column, whether it is required, and what it holds.

00:02:32.271 --> 00:02:36.961
Here the title is required, and the email, city and plan are optional.

00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:42.692
A column named ContentItemId lets a row update an item that already exists,

00:02:42.692 --> 00:02:45.025
instead of creating a new one.

00:02:49.277 --> 00:02:52.280
Choose your file with the file picker.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.307
This one is a list of customers, saved as a CSV file.

00:02:56.797 --> 00:03:02.450
Publish imported content is ticked, so every item is published as soon as it is imported.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.497
Untick it to save each item as a draft that you publish later.

00:03:07.023 --> 00:03:08.259
Click Upload.

00:03:08.259 --> 00:03:13.982
A progress bar shows the upload, and a large file is sent in pieces automatically.

00:03:13.982 --> 00:03:16.453
Then the Bulk Import page opens.

00:03:20.626 --> 00:03:24.401
The import is now a row on the Bulk Import page, with the

00:03:24.401 --> 00:03:29.436
file name, the content type, its status, the person who uploaded it, and when.

00:03:29.897 --> 00:03:33.576
It runs in the background, so you can leave the page.

00:03:33.576 --> 00:03:38.877
When it is done, the status reads Completed, or Completed with errors, as here.

00:03:39.372 --> 00:03:44.003
The green number is how many records were imported, and the red number

00:03:44.003 --> 00:03:45.952
is how many were rejected.

00:03:45.952 --> 00:03:48.755
A rejected row does not stop the others:

00:03:48.755 --> 00:03:52.472
here, the rows without a title did not pass validation.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:54.726
Open the Actions menu.

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:59.834
Download errors gives you only the rejected rows, in the same file format,

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.813
with the reason for each.

00:04:01.813 --> 00:04:04.559
Fix them, and import that file again.

00:04:05.184 --> 00:04:10.303
While an import runs, Pause import stops it, and Resume import continues from

00:04:10.303 --> 00:04:11.844
the last saved row.

00:04:11.844 --> 00:04:18.074
Delete removes the entry and its uploaded file, but never the content items that were imported.

00:04:18.566 --> 00:04:23.108
The Show menu lists only the imports with one status, such as Paused

00:04:23.108 --> 00:04:27.466
or Failed, and the Sort menu puts the newest or the oldest first.

00:04:27.918 --> 00:04:33.140
The imported customers are now content items of the site, ready to edit,

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.818
publish and search like any other.

00:04:40.118 --> 00:04:45.298
On the Bulk Export page, click Export to open the Export contents form.

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:50.270
Choose the File type, CSV or Excel, and then the Content type.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:55.179
The Export Data button stays disabled until a content type is chosen.

00:04:55.948 --> 00:04:59.531
Export scope is Export all published by default.

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:03.048
Choose Filtered Export to narrow the file down.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:08.483
Filter Options limit the export to a range of Created or Modified dates,

00:05:08.483 --> 00:05:12.763
or to the Owners you type, as user names separated by commas.

00:05:12.763 --> 00:05:18.960
Published only, Latest only and All versions choose which versions of each item to include.

00:05:22.062 --> 00:05:23.468
Click Export Data.

00:05:23.468 --> 00:05:26.106
A small export downloads straight away.

00:05:26.106 --> 00:05:30.267
A large one is prepared in the background, and the page tells you

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.732
it has been queued.

00:05:32.219 --> 00:05:37.129
When the export is ready, its row shows Completed, the number of records,

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:38.869
and a Download button.

00:05:39.327 --> 00:05:43.278
The file uses the same column names as an import template.

00:05:43.278 --> 00:05:47.723
So you can export, change the file in a spreadsheet, and import it

00:05:47.723 --> 00:05:50.007
again to update the same items.

00:05:54.207 --> 00:05:58.256
What a person sees depends on the permissions of their role.

00:05:58.256 --> 00:06:03.347
List content transfer entries shows the Import menu and the Bulk Import page.

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:10.817
Import content items from file allows uploading files, downloading templates and error files,

00:06:10.817 --> 00:06:13.532
and pausing or resuming an import.

00:06:13.532 --> 00:06:17.062
Export content items from file allows exports.

00:06:17.062 --> 00:06:20.727
Delete content transfer entries removes entries.

00:06:21.477 --> 00:06:26.471
Each import and export permission also exists for a single content type, so

00:06:26.471 --> 00:06:29.616
a role can import customers and nothing else.

00:06:29.616 --> 00:06:32.637
Administrators have all of them by default.

00:06:33.387 --> 00:06:38.074
Your technical team can keep the uploaded and exported files in Azure Blob

00:06:38.074 --> 00:06:41.941
Storage, so a site that runs on several servers shares them.

00:06:41.941 --> 00:06:44.167
That needs no screen of its own.

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:54.467
Load a purchased or partner list of leads, customers or products in a single upload.

00:06:55.217 --> 00:06:57.609
Move records from another system:

00:06:57.609 --> 00:07:00.737
export them there, then import the file here.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:04.037
Correct many records at once.

00:07:04.037 --> 00:07:09.937
Export them, fix the file in Excel, and import it to update the same items.

00:07:10.687 --> 00:07:15.347
Hand a list to an accountant or a partner who has no access to the site.

00:07:17.347 --> 00:07:22.063
Bulk import and export turn a spreadsheet into content, and content into a

00:07:22.063 --> 00:07:25.364
spreadsheet, with every row checked on the way in.

00:07:25.364 --> 00:07:26.897
Thanks for watching.

